title A lap that came back out of the stash
prompt the baton -- take the next agent-doable lap, reds first
think The open answered no dirty index and four stashes, the newest stamped 20260907.155144 -- eight minutes old, this seat's own, thirteen files including a written session log. That is %321's shape exactly: a dead lap leaves no dirty index, its leavings are stashed, and a stash is neither tree nor index. The work was proven and unlanded, so recovering it beat starting anything new.
think git stash pop returned all thirteen and left two conflicts. The fold recital is append-only, so both hands' lines stand -- a merge that drops either is a record with a hole in it. The card conflicted on a whole block: my parked lap had condensed COPAL to make room, and COPAL had published a newer block of its own meanwhile, so the condensation was aimed at prose that no longer stood. I took upstream whole and dropped my own side, which is the derived spine's rule read one artifact over -- a published thing does not move for an unpublished one.
think Then the bill arrived. The hot roster answered guards_red=10 over 173 guards, and not one of the ten was a fault in the recovered work. Two were the index still holding the conflicted files as unmerged, which exec_bit reads as mode 000000. Two were the REDS headline census disagreeing with a spine that had gained a row. One was a shelf row a rebase had left out of order, %440's twelfth firing. One was three links in a new shelf still carrying the card's depth into archive/. One was the card 480 bytes over its own bound. One was a rung-mark ceiling the card's own extra prose had crossed by four.
think The tenth is the one worth keeping. instrument_refusal read a swallowed instrument in the very file the recovered work repaired -- and the repair is what made it visible. The elder line wrote to a constant /tmp path, so the guard's redirect test did not match it; moving the write into a private mktemp pen brought the line inside the predicate. A repair uncovering an elder fault beneath it is the happiest way to meet one.
think Removing the swallow then found a second thing underneath. With 2>/dev/null and || true taken off, awk refused by name on expanding-prompts/yonder/cursor-prompt_reorg-chunk-3_external-research (1).md -- one tracked page whose name carries a space, word-split by a for f in $(git ls-files ...) loop and therefore never read by this scan in its whole life. The swallow had been hiding a reading gap rather than a transient failure, which is exactly what a swallow is for.
obs The mechanism, plainly. tools/fixtures/s/shipped_binary_claim_scan.sh replaces its bare-invocation loop: the page list is written to the pen and read with while IFS= read -r rather than word-split from a command substitution, and the awk pass drops 2>/dev/null and || true, refusing with instrument=failed and verdict=misread when the reader breaks. construction/ITINERARY.md carries a new INCENSE block and a condensed %499 pointer; construction/CHECKPOINTS.md carries the cairn for that condensation, replacing the 20260907.154440 one whose sweep the stash pop undid.
obs The finding, and it is a fleet number rather than a seat's. %499 has now cost this seat two laps and COPAL one, today. The recovery took six repairs no author wrote, in five files, none of them a defect in the work being recovered -- so the honest cost of a park is not the round it delays, it is the arithmetic a later hand pays to put a correct tree back together around it. A park keeps every byte and still costs the lap; what this lap measures is that it costs the NEXT one too.
obs What I did not take, and why. The discriminator %499 needs is one local test -- the merge-base equals the parent of the oldest commit in xy/main..HEAD exactly when the local line's base still stands upstream -- and it is four lines. Six ships run fleet_round_open.sh, and a mistake in it is a fleet that cannot open a round. That is a shape decision at fleet scale rather than a lap, and it stays Keaton's.
obs The parked log is corrected rather than reprinted. Its status line claimed sent, which was true of every word but that one; an unlanded log is still being written, so the line now says what happened and two obs lines name the correction. BAKERY made the same move on 20260907.135743 for the same cause, which is what makes it a practice rather than a liberty.
loom roster=hot guards=173 green=160 red=10 gated=3 wall_s=1219
loom recovery=stash_pop files=13 conflicts=2 repairs_no_author_wrote=6
loom card=ITINERARY bytes_before=41440 bound=40960 bytes_after=40927
loom scan=shipped_binary_claim pages_unread_by_word_split=1 swallowed_instrument_passes=1
rota lap 4192, row 2 -- Fire, the row that sees; its threshold asks what must stop and what must be cut, and the lap's whole shape was looking straight at a stash nobody wanted to open rather than starting fresh work beside it.
file tools/fixtures/s/shipped_binary_claim_scan.sh the swallow removed, the refusal named, and the page list read without word-splitting
file construction/ITINERARY.md the recovery account, the %499 block condensed to a pointer with every question kept
file construction/CHECKPOINTS.md the cairn for that condensation, replacing one whose sweep the stash pop undid
file construction/REDS.md the headline census rewritten to the spine the recovered row joined
file construction/archive/20260907-154440_itinerary-landed-accounts.md three shelf links repaired to the shelf's own depth, and the condensed %499 block held whole
file session-logs/date/20260907/20260907-154925_a-wipe-read-as-a-flag.kyri the parked lap's own record, its status line corrected to what happened
file session-logs/date/README-index-20260907.md the misordered row sorted, %440's twelfth firing
scope one lap: recover a parked round whole, close the ten reds its landing raised, and measure what the park cost
status landed, roster hot green, sent
recommend check-in (Keaton) -- one question and it is the same one twice over. %499's discriminator is four lines and would have spared this seat two laps and COPAL one in a single day; it lives in a file six ships run, so seating it is yours rather than mine. The two from the recovered round stand beside it: may a lap repair a shared pen in a lane whose witness it cannot run, and may rule_twin's drift ceiling become a floor on agreement.
